        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T07:52:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is it possible gpa \u003c kvm-\u003earch.pkvm.pvmfw_load_addr? Seems range_has_pvmfw() allows this case.",
      "revId": "df73329d09c37d048afaf19e48bae1d52cc86fe1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "35ffbe99_d1a28806",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T17:14:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Indeed, seems so. More precisely, range_has_pvmfw() doesn\u0027t check if `pkvm-\u003epvmfw_load_addr + pvmfw_size` doesn\u0027t overflow. So it may return true even with gpa_end \u003c gpa_start.\n\nThis logic is basically just copied from ARM\u0027s pkvm_ipa_range_has_pvmfw() and pkvm_load_pvmfw_pages().\n\nWhat\u0027s interesting is that this pvmfw_load_addr value comes from the host (even from userspace), and we don\u0027t validate it. :) \n\nIn pKVM-ARM it is not validated either: \nhost: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/0c79caf88acb1b7af67e8e4cc42f9f8aa35a291f/arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c#906\nhypervisor: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/0c79caf88acb1b7af67e8e4cc42f9f8aa35a291f/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c#612\n\nSo it may well be U64_MAX - PAGE_SIZE + 1 or whatever.\n\nI suppose this will not cause anything bad in practice, for various reasons, but it would be probably cleaner to prevent this explicitly.\n\ncc @willdeacon@google.com",
      "parentUuid": "300b82d9_3b06631c",
      "revId": "df73329d09c37d048afaf19e48bae1d52cc86fe1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3393dd1_3fbdb16e",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-25T00:43:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "not just the overflow case, but also the cases `gpa_start \u003c pvmfw_load_addr \u003c gpa_end \u003c pvmfw_load_end` and `gpa_start \u003c pvmfw_load_addr \u003c pvmfw_load_end \u003c gpa_end`. Seems these cases don\u0027t need `pkvm-\u003epvmfw_load_addr + pvmfw_size` overflow, and can also pass the check of `range_has_pvmfw()`.",
      "parentUuid": "35ffbe99_d1a28806",
      "revId": "df73329d09c37d048afaf19e48bae1d52cc86fe1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5667c52_c88cfc50",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-25T13:18:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah indeed, since range_has_pvmfw() just checks if the range overlaps with pvmfw, not necessarily contains it...\n\nSo, if gpa \u003c pvmfw_load_addr, in most cases `offset` will be a large number that won\u0027t pass the below `offset \u003e\u003d pvmfw_size` check, so we will not copy anything. But that seems to be precisely a problem, since we do want to copy the overlapping part of pvmfw.\n\nI imagine this might be a real issue, for instance, on ARM with 16K pages with THP, since the pvmfw start address 0x7FC00000 in the crosvm memory map (https://crosvm.dev/book/appendix/memory_layout.htmlhttps://crosvm.dev/book/appendix/memory_layout.html) is not aligned to 32MB, so IIUC if the faulted-in page is a huge page then:\n\nipa \u003d 0x7e000000\npvmfw_load_addr \u003d 0x7fc00000\noffset \u003d 0xfffffffffe400000\npvmfw_size \u003d 0x400000\n\nso pvmfw is not gonna be loaded? (Adding more pKVM-ARM folks.)\n\nAnyway, it seems the cleanest solution would be to let range_has_pvmfw() itself return the overlapped range and the pvmfw offset.",
      "parentUuid": "a3393dd1_3fbdb16e",
      "revId": "df73329d09c37d048afaf19e48bae1d52cc86fe1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd650d95_715a1c35",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-25T17:18:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that looks like a bug introduced when we added support for huge-pages. @vdonnefort@google.com can you file a bug so we can get this fixed, please?",
      "parentUuid": "c5667c52_c88cfc50",
      "revId": "df73329d09c37d048afaf19e48bae1d52cc86fe1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46b13921_34f9b70c",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
