        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T08:37:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Checking if size is page aligned is probably redundant: in pkvm_firmware_rmem_init we\u0027ve already made sure that pvmfw size is page aligned and taking into account that size passed to this function comes from guest_mmu_map_leaf and pgt_level_to_size ensures it is page aligned as well. But I think it is better to keep it as is even if redundant - just a side comment.\n\nBTW looking at it I just realized that when userspace sets pvmfw load addr via KVM_CAP_X86_PROTECTED_VM_FLAGS_SET_FW_GPA, we do not check if it is page aligned in pkvm_vm_ioctl_set_fw_gpa but perhaps we should? Seems like it is not a security issue to allow user-space setting arbitrary non-aligned address but in such case entire page will be donated to guest anyway and potentially waste some memory. WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 104,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 105,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "df73329d09c37d048afaf19e48bae1d52cc86fe1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8f7eceb_fa091bfd",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 105,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T17:14:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e taking into account that size passed to this function comes from guest_mmu_map_leaf and pgt_level_to_size ensures it is page aligned as well.\n\nI hope we will get rid of guest_mmu_map_leaf() and will call this directly instead, then it will not be ensured so automatically anymore.\n\n\u003e BTW looking at it I just realized that when userspace sets pvmfw load addr via KVM_CAP_X86_PROTECTED_VM_FLAGS_SET_FW_GPA, we do not check if it is page aligned in pkvm_vm_ioctl_set_fw_gpa but perhaps we should? Seems like it is not a security issue to allow user-space setting arbitrary non-aligned address but in such case entire page will be donated to guest anyway and potentially waste some memory. WDYT?\n\nI agree, but I\u0027ll also let @willdeacon@google.com speak, since this logic, as well as the ioctl implementation, is basically just copied from pKVM-ARM. :)",
      "parentUuid": "6d2dbb73_cb307c68",
